  message: "BAKEOFF VALIDATION: INCONCLUSIVE — tag KEPT, structural cohort gap, third\nconsecutive time. All 8 reflect assessments (deep-20260717-200119) returned\ninconclusive with the same reason: this cohort contains ZERO Python\nargparse CLI targets (go/js/ts/python-django/csharp/java/swift/rust — the\none Python repo, pretix, uses Django management commands, already detected\nas cli_command). No cohort rerun can validate this claim; it needs a\nDIRECTED probe: run the pipeline on a repo with a real argparse CLI (any\npython package exposing console_scripts + argparse subcommands) and check\nthe subprocess linker's concept keying per the item's fix (dev 2e9611808f,\nmerged 2026-07-02). That is minutes of work against a purpose-picked repo,\nnot a bakeoff slot."  # 97b2
- op: discuss  # a677
  at: '2026-08-01T20:40:28Z'  # a677
  by: agent  # a677
  actor: jgstern_agent  # a677
  clock: 8  # a677
  nonce: a677  # a677
  message: "DIRECTED PROBE: no_move. Tag KEPT (the no_move lifecycle keeps the parent tagged). Fourth\nvalidation attempt, and the FIRST one that is not a cohort gap.\n\nRan the full pipeline on hypergumbo itself, the canonical example this item names:\n  hypergumbo survey /home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo --out /tmp/hg_self/survey.json\n    --no-sketch-fan-out --no-handler-slices --no-progress\nexit 0, 7m53s. Independently recounted from the artifact: 41448 nodes, 140086 edges,\nsubprocess_calls edges = 0, subprocess_cli call-site symbols = 90. The linker RAN and joined\nnothing.\n\nBoth halves of the qualifying construct are present in this repo (each line read back from\nsource, not taken from the probe report):\n  (a) cli.py:7535-7536 p_slice = sub.add_parser(\"slice\", ...) ; cli.py:7683\n      p_slice.set_defaults(func=cmd_slice) ; handler at cli.py:1602 def cmd_slice(...).\n      26 such add_parser/set_defaults pairs in total.\n  (b) scripts/hypergumbo_diag.py:960 subprocess.run([\"hypergumbo\", \"slice\", \"--input\", in_path,\n      ...], capture_output=True, check=True) -- verified present, and the file is inside the\n      linker's own scan scope.\nSo this is a genuine no_move, not a fifth \"no cohort repo has the construct\".\n\nTHE WI-lubap FIX ITSELF IS SOUND -- measured separately and labelled as PREREQUISITE-ONLY\nevidence, which does NOT satisfy the behavioral claim: production _scan_argparse_commands run\nagainst the 41448 real survey symbols resolves 26 subcommands to 27 handler symbols, matching\n26/26 of the subcommands that hypergumbo --help lists, with concept=command = 0. The requirement\ndiagnostic this item asked for reads 27 where it read 0 pre-fix.\n\nTHE ZERO COMES FROM TWO OTHER DEFECTS, both upstream of the argparse join, each sufficient alone,\nplus one latent third. Filed as a separate untagged item (see the follow-up note below):\n  B1 linkers/subprocess_cli.py:131-201 _detect_project_cli_name, guard at :616. Reads only\n     <repo_root>/pyproject.toml. hypergumbo's monorepo root has no [project] table; the console\n     script is declared in packages/hypergumbo/pyproject.toml. Verified live:\n     _detect_project_cli_name(Path(\"/home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo\")) returns set(). The guard\n     \"call.executable in project_cli_names\" can therefore never pass, for any call, ever.\n  B2 subprocess_cli.py:98 ast.literal_eval with the swallow at :127-128. It literal_evals the\n     ENTIRE argv list, so one non-literal element drops the whole call site. The diag call at\n     :960 contains in_path / node_id_val / str(max_hops) / str(max_files) / out_path, raises\n     ValueError, and the site is never recorded -- the regex matches, the extraction does not.\n     The swallowing branch carries a no-cover pragma while demonstrably executing on our own\n     source.\n  B3 (latent, would emit a WRONG edge once B1/B2 are fixed) subprocess_cli.py:410-412 / :440-442.\n     _scan_argparse_commands indexes handlers by BARE NAME with no kind or path filter, unlike\n     _scan_fire_commands which enforces same-file scoping. On this repo \"survey\" resolves to both\n     the real cmd_run and an external_symbol placeholder, and the min-by-id tie-break picks the\n     placeholder.\n\nWHY NO BAKEOFF WILL EVER MOVE THIS: 501 repo roots under ALL_REPOS were scanned with the\nproduction scanning functions. 8 have at least one argparse subcommand->handler pair; 0 have the\njoint construct. 6 of those 8 have neither a root pyproject.toml nor a setup.py, so B1 zeroes\nthem by construction. The re-validation instrument after B1/B2/B3 land should be THIS directed\nprobe, not a cohort slot: re-run the survey on this repo and assert at least one subprocess_calls\nedge from scripts/hypergumbo_diag.py:960 to cmd_slice carrying the subcommand in meta."  # a677
